From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mv88e6xxx: pulse the reset line before detection

On the Gigaset Maxwell 10, the 88E6320 reference clock comes from the DECT
chip (DVF99). Released from reset before that clock is stable, the switch
stays mute on MDIO and single-chip detection fails with -ENODEV; the
driver only toggles reset after a successful detection. Request the line
asserted, then release it and wait before detecting.

Verified by hand: a 20 ms pulse on GPIO1_IO09 makes the switch answer
(ID 0x1152) and DSA probes.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c b/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c
index 284270a4a..88ab7dce6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c
@@ -7223,13 +7223,21 @@ static int mv88e6xxx_probe(struct mdio_device *mdiodev)
 
 	chip->info = compat_info;
 
-	chip->reset = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	/* Request the reset line asserted and pulse it before detection: a
+	 * switch released from reset before its reference clock was stable
+	 * (here supplied by another chip) stays mute on MDIO, and the regular
+	 * hardware reset only happens after a successful detection.
+	 */
+	chip->reset = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(chip->reset)) {
 		err = PTR_ERR(chip->reset);
 		goto out;
 	}
-	if (chip->reset)
+	if (chip->reset) {
 		usleep_range(10000, 20000);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(chip->reset, 0);
+		msleep(50);
+	}
 
 	/* Detect if the device is configured in single chip addressing mode,
 	 * otherwise continue with address specific smi init/detection.
